.TH POTOK 1 "2026-10-24" "Potok 0.3.3"
.SH NAME
potok \- terminal BitTorrent client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B potok
.RI [ options ] " [SOURCE]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Potok provides a terminal interface to its own background BitTorrent worker.
Closing the interface leaves downloads and uploads running.
An external Transmission service is not required.
An optional SOURCE is a local torrent path, magnet link or HTTP(S) torrent URL.
It is added before opening the interface. Quote paths containing spaces;
use -- before a filename beginning with a dash.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --background
Start the worker without opening the interface.
.TP
.B --status
Print the worker PID and torrent count. Exit with status 1 if it is not running.
.TP
.B --stop
Save torrent state and stop the worker.
.TP
.BI --lang " en|ru"
Select the interface language for this invocation.
.TP
.BI --download-dir " DIR"
Override the destination for new downloads.
.TP
.BI --state-dir " DIR"
Select the worker profile. The directory must be private to the current user.
.TP
.BI --config-dir " DIR"
Select the configuration directory.
.TP
.B --demo
Show an animated preview without network or configuration changes.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version.
.TP
.B --help
Print usage.
.SH KEYS
.B a
opens the add form;
.B f
opens file search;
.B Ctrl-F
opens file search from the add form.
Use Tab to switch fields, Enter to submit, and Esc to cancel.
.B p
pauses or resumes;
.B l
switches EN/RU;
.B ?
opens help.
.B d
or
.B D
opens the removal dialog. Leave "Delete downloaded files" unchecked to keep
data, or check it with Space or the mouse to delete complete and partial
downloads. Enter confirms; Esc cancels. Data deletion bypasses the recycle bin.
.B q
closes the interface while downloads continue.
.B Q
stops downloads after confirmation.
.SH FILES
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/potok/config
or
.I ~/.config/potok/config
stores language, download_dir, state_dir, and browse_dir.
The default browse_dir is the home directory and does not change when a file
is selected. A directory typed in the source field scopes one file search.
.PP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/potok
or
.I ~/.local/share/potok
stores resume data, speed limits, the control socket, and worker.log.
.SH NOTES
fzf is optional; a built-in file picker is available without it.
The terminal supplies the background color and transparency.
No boot-time service is installed.
